<title>FRANCE: France sells 21.51 bln Ffr BTANs at auction.</title>
<headline>France sells 21.51 bln Ffr BTANs at auction.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following tap stock (BTAN) issues were announced by the Treasury after today's auction.</p>
<p> MATURITY	COUPON	SALE AMOUNT     AVERAGE YIELD</p>
<p> 12.APR.99	4.75	  9.53 BLN	  3.63 PCT</p>
<p> BID AMT/COVER    NON-COMPETITIVE BIDS   LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE</p>
<p> 29.00 BLN/3.0     NIL			   101.96</p>
<p> PCT ALLOTED AT LOWEST PRICE*		  PAYMENT DATE</p>
<p> 30.00						   05.JUN</p>
<p>* PRICES ABOVE GOT ALLOTMENTS IN FULL  </p>
<p> MATURITY	COUPON	SALE AMOUNT     AVERAGE YIELD</p>
<p> 12 MAR.02	4.75	   11.98 BLN	4.59 PCT</p>
<p> BID AMT/COVER    NON-COMPETITIVE BIDS   LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE</p>
<p> 29.18 BLN/2.4		   432 MLN	  100.63</p>
<p> PCT ALLOTED AT LOWEST PRICE*		  PAYMENT DATE</p>
<p> 100 PCT						 12.JUN</p>
<p>* PRICES ABOVE GOT ALLOTMENTS IN FULL</p>
<p>NOTE - The Treasury originally announced it would sell 20 to 22 billion francs of BTANs in total on Thursday. The total bid cover ratio of the auction was 2.4.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 54 52</p>
</text>
